@ohnoov It's unfortunate that you hit this. That's not how the warning meant to be (i.e. old PID1 setting up v1 and new one breaking).

> Edge case of not updating initramfs often enough, I guess.

It seems that [pacman doesn't automate that](https://gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/mkinitcpio/mkinitcpio/-/blob/master/libalpm/hooks/90-mkinitcpio-install.hook?ref_type=heads#L15). I'd suggest adding a hook there to keep systemd binaries in sync. (Also, what was the version within the initrd? [This](https://gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/packaging/packages/systemd/-/commit/d0f176adf66205e864e85bf34cdccb3329d308ab#9b9baac1eb9b72790eef5540a1685306fc43fd6c_122_120) suggests it must have been <=v247.)
